{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And to set you high above all the nations which He has made, for praise</b> — that all the peoples of the earth will praise you, given that YHWH is near in all your calling to Him." "<b>And for a name</b> — that a name will go forth for you among the nations through the splendor that He has placed upon you, for you are exalted above them all." "<b>And for glory</b> — for you shall glory over them to do with them all that you desire; you shall decree a thing and it shall be established for you, as in the manner of \"lest Israel glory over me, saying, 'My hand has saved me'\" (Judges 7:2)." "<b>And to make you a holy people</b> — to cleave to Him in the end. And by way of truth: לתהלה (for praise), for the Elohim of Israel — He is your praise, and His great Name — He is your Elohim, and in this is your glory, as in the manner of what is said: \"For the glory of their strength are You\" (Psalms 89:18), \"The glory of Israel\" (Lamentations 2:1)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {3 "The kabbalistic passage is rendered hyper-literally without expansion, per the way-of-truth rule. The ellipsis of Elohim in 'He is your praise' follows the Hebrew syntax faithfully."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:56:21.170714996Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}